/E (Born December 5,1942, in Narva, Estonia, John and his family fled Estonia in 1944 as the Soviet Army advanced. They eventually reached a Displaced Persons \(DP\) camp in American-controlled Geislingen, Germany. In 1950, his family was able to secure a church sponsor in Oklahoma City. They came to America by ship and spent three years in Oklahoma City before moving to Hempstead, Long Island.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
